---
description: Keep short summaries at the high-level function of a capability
alwaysApply: true
---

# Short summaries

A short summary names the high-level function of a command or capability. That includes CLI help text, the README command list, and any other one-line description.

Leave each specific behavior, option, and sub-feature out of that line. Those details belong in requirements and in longer documentation.

```markdown
<!-- Bad: the line inventories one behavior of format -->
- `shallgraph format` - rewrite requirement YAML into canonical format. Markdown tables in refinement, claim text, and rationale are column-aligned.

<!-- Good: the line names the job -->
- `shallgraph format` - rewrite requirement YAML into canonical format.
```

Adding a behavior to an existing capability does not add a clause to its short summary.
